(- allocate_vehicle_unit)
(- attach_task_profile)
(- confirm_candidate_preparedness (makes candidate_prepared))
(- activate_origin_node / activate_destination_node (makes node ready))
(- assign_operator_resource (makes candidate_operator_linked))
(- lock_origin_availability / lock_destination_availability (makes locked and confirmed))
(- (optional) release_operator_resource after lock (to free operator for next use))
(Now after both origin and destination locked and confirmed, we can assemble transport leg (assemble_transport_leg). This requires origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_availability_node_linked, destination_availability_node_linked, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available.)
(All those will be true after lock steps.)
(Effect: transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_origin_linked, transport_leg_destination_linked, not transport_leg_available.)
(Now we need to authorize transport leg loading: authorize_transport_leg_loading requires transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, not transport_leg_loading_authorized.)
(We have origin_availability_locked true, transport_leg_assembled true, we need candidate_task_profile_linked for origin_availability (we attached earlier). So we can authorize.)
(Effect: transport_leg_loading_authorized.)
(Now we need to load container onto leg: loading_container_onto_leg requires candidate_prepared ?candidate (sb), candidate_transport_leg_linked ?candidate ?transport_leg (we have that from init), candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container (we have loading_container_beta linked to sb from init), loading_container_available ?loading_container (we have loading_container_beta available initially), transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg (true), transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_leg (true), not loading_container_loaded ?loading_container.)
(Thus we can load container (either alpha or beta). Since sb is linked to loading_container_beta, we should load that container. So we load loading_container_beta onto transport_leg_alpha.)
(Effect: loading_container_loaded ?loading_container, loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, not loading_container_available.)
(Now we need to stage schedule candidate: stage_schedule_candidate requires candidate_prepared ?candidate, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_loaded ?loading_container, loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, not origin_leg_loaded ?transport_leg, not candidate_staged_for_loading ?candidate.)
(We have candidate_prepared sb (we will have done that earlier), candidate_loading_container_linked sb loading_container_beta (init), loading_container_loaded loading_container_beta (just loaded), loading_container_leg_linked loading_container_beta transport_leg_alpha (effect from loading), candidate_task_profile_linked sb route_task_profile_alpha (we will attach), not origin_leg_loaded (we haven't done origin_leg_loaded; we only assembled leg without loading origin/destination). So origin_leg_loaded is false. Not candidate_staged_for_loading sb (we haven't staged yet). So we can stage sb.)
(Effect: candidate_staged_for_loading sb (goal satisfied).)
(Now we need to assign operator and skill certificate to sb. We can do that before or after staging; doesn't matter.)
(We also need to ensure compliance_certificate_alpha is available at end. We'll not assign it to anyone.)
(Now we need to dispatch shift_candidate_alpha (sa). For that we need:)
(- create_candidate sa)
(- allocate_vehicle_unit sa ?vehicle)
(- attach_task_profile sa route_task_profile_alpha)
(- confirm_candidate_preparedness sa)
(- assign_operator_resource sa ?operator (maybe we can reuse operator after releasing))
(- assign_skill_certificate? Not needed for sa.)
(- Maybe assign compliance certificate? Not needed.)
(- Then allocate dispatch slot: allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate requires dispatch_ready ?candidate, candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot, not dispatch_allocated ?candidate.)
(- To get dispatch_ready ?candidate, we need either finalize_candidate_direct or finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation or finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation or mark_origin/destination_dispatch_ready? Actually dispatch_ready is a predicate that can be set by finalize_candidate_direct, finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation, finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation, mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready, mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready, maybe also execute_*_dispatch? No, those produce dispatched not dispatch_ready. So we need to make sa dispatch_ready.)
(We can use finalize_candidate_direct (requires candidate_clearance_established ?candidate, not route_sequence_context_set ?candidate, not candidate_finalized ?candidate). That seems simpler: we need candidate_clearance_established sa and not route_sequence_context_set sa. We can establish clearance via establish_clearance_* actions. Those require candidate_loading_verified ?candidate, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked ?candidate ?compliance_certificate, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, plus conditions on origin_leg_loaded/destination_leg_loaded.)
(Thus to get clearance we need to have loading verified and compliance certificate linked, plus loading container linked and leg linked, plus either origin_leg_loaded, destination_leg_loaded, both, or none depending on which clearance action we choose.)
(We have not yet loaded any container onto leg for sa; we could load container onto leg for sa as well (maybe using loading_container_alpha). But we need to have origin_leg_loaded or destination_leg_loaded or none. For establish_clearance_nominal we need not origin_leg_loaded and not destination_leg_loaded. So we could load container onto leg (loading_container_loaded) but not set origin_leg_loaded nor destination_leg_loaded. However loading_container_onto_leg does not set those. So we can load container onto leg (any container) and then use establish_clearance_nominal (which requires not origin_leg_loaded and not destination_leg_loaded). That would work.)
(Thus for sa we need:)
(- candidate_prepared sa (we will have))
(- candidate_loading_container_linked sa ?loading_container (we have loading_container_alpha linked to sa from init))
(- loading_container_available ?loading_container (we have loading_container_alpha available initially))
(- transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg (we need to assemble leg for sa as well))
(- transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_leg (need to authorize))
(- loading_container_loaded ?loading_container (after loading))
(- loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg (after loading))
(- candidate_loading_verified ?candidate (need to verify loading profile))
(- candidate_compliance_certificate_linked ?candidate ?compliance_certificate (we must not use compliance certificate for sa if we want it available at end for goal? Actually goal requires compliance_certificate_available compliance_certificate_alpha. So we cannot link it to any candidate. So we cannot use compliance certificate for sa. But establish_clearance_nominal requires candidate_compliance_certificate_linked ?candidate ?compliance_certificate. So we cannot use that action if we want to keep compliance certificate available. However we could use establish_clearance_origin_loaded or destination_loaded or full_load, which also require candidate_compliance_certificate_linked. All clearance actions require candidate_compliance_certificate_linked. So to get clearance we must link compliance certificate to the candidate. That would make it not available, violating goal. However maybe we can release the compliance certificate after establishing clearance? There is action release_compliance_certificate that takes ?candidate - schedule_candidate ?compliance_certificate - compliance_certificate. Precondition: candidate_compliance_certificate_linked ?candidate ?compliance_certificate. Effect: compliance_certificate_available ?compliance_certificate, not candidate_compliance_certificate_linked ?candidate ?compliance_certificate. So we could link compliance certificate to sa, establish clearance, then release it, making it available again. The goal requires compliance_certificate_available at the end, so we can release after establishing clearance.)
(Thus we can use compliance certificate for sa, then release it.)
(Thus steps for sa:)
(- allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm preparedness.)
(- allocate operator? Not needed for clearance but maybe for other steps? Not required.)
(- assign compliance_certificate to sa (assign_compliance_certificate))
(- load container onto leg (need transport leg assembled and authorized))
(- verify loading profile (need candidate_loading_verified). There are two verify actions: verify_loading_profile_nominal (requires not destination_leg_loaded) and verify_loading_profile_destination_flag (requires destination_leg_loaded). Since we haven't loaded destination leg, we can use verify_loading_profile_nominal.)
(- establish clearance: we can use establish_clearance_nominal (requires not origin_leg_loaded and not destination_leg_loaded). Since we haven't loaded origin or destination leg, that works.)
(- Then release compliance certificate.)
(- Then finalize_candidate_direct (requires candidate_clearance_established, not route_sequence_context_set, not candidate_finalized). We'll have clearance established, not route_sequence_context_set (we haven't set it), not candidate_finalized. So we can finalize directly.)
(- Then allocate dispatch slot (requires dispatch_ready). After finalize_candidate_direct, effect includes dispatch_ready ?candidate. So we can allocate dispatch slot.)
(- Then execute_schedule_dispatch (requires dispatch_allocated ?candidate, candidate_vehicle_linked ?candidate ?vehicle_unit, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?candidate ?dispatch_slot, not dispatched ?candidate). We'll have allocated vehicle earlier, and after allocate_dispatch_slot we have candidate_dispatch_slot_linked. So we can dispatch.)
(Alternatively we could use finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation which requires route_sequence_validated, but that requires more steps (service window, validate route sequence). We'll avoid that for simplicity.)
(Thus for sa we need to assemble transport leg, authorize loading, load container, verify loading, establish clearance, release compliance, finalize, allocate dispatch slot, dispatch.)
(Now for origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha dispatch:)
(We need to dispatch them via execute_origin_dispatch and execute_destination_dispatch.)
(Those actions require dispatch_allocated ?origin_availability, candidate_vehicle_linked ?origin_availability ?vehicle_unit, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?origin_availability ?dispatch_slot, not dispatched ?origin_availability.)
(Thus we need to:)
(- create_candidate oa, da)
(- allocate vehicle to each)
(- attach_task_profile to each)
(- confirm_candidate_preparedness (makes candidate_prepared))
(- assign operator resource to each (needed for lock actions later? Actually for dispatch we don't need operator linked; dispatch actions do not require operator. However we need operator for lock actions if we need to lock them for transport leg assembly (for sb). So we need to assign operator to oa and da for lock steps.)
(- activate origin node and destination node (makes nodes ready))
(- lock origin_availability and destination_availability (makes them locked and confirmed))
(- After locking, we have origin_availability_locked and origin_availability_confirmed, destination similarly.)
(- Then we need to allocate dispatch slot to oa and da? Actually execute_origin_dispatch requires dispatch_allocated ?origin_availability. So we need to allocate a dispatch slot to oa. Similarly for da. We have only one dispatch slot, but we can reuse after each dispatch (the action makes slot available). So we can allocate slot to oa, dispatch oa, slot becomes free, allocate to da, dispatch da, slot free, allocate to sa, dispatch sa.)
(- For each dispatch we also need candidate_vehicle_linked to a vehicle unit. We'll need to allocate a vehicle to each candidate before dispatch. After dispatch, vehicle becomes available again (effect includes vehicle_available). So we can reuse vehicles.)
(Thus we need to allocate vehicle to oa, dispatch oa, release vehicle, allocate vehicle to da, dispatch da, release vehicle, allocate vehicle to sa, dispatch sa.)
(We also need to attach task profile to each candidate (oa, da, sa, sb). We'll need to do that before confirm_candidate_preparedness.)
(We also need to assign operator to oa and da for lock steps (we can assign, lock, release operator). For sb we also need operator link (goal). So we need to assign operator to sb and keep it linked (goal requires candidate_operator_linked sb op). So we should not release operator from sb after linking.)
(Thus we need to assign operator to oa, lock oa, release operator; assign operator to da, lock da, release operator; assign operator to sb (and keep). That uses operator three times but we can reuse after releasing.)
(Now we need to also assign skill certificate to sb (goal). So assign_skill_certificate sb skill.)
(Now we need to load container onto leg for sb (as described) and stage sb.)
(We also need to load container onto leg for sa? Actually for sa we need to load container onto leg to verify loading and establish clearance. We'll need to load a container onto leg for sa as well. We have loading_container_alpha linked to sa from init. So we can load that.)
(Thus we need to assemble transport leg for sa as well? Actually we need transport leg assembled and loading authorized for sa's loading container onto leg. However we already assembled transport leg for sb? The transport leg is the same object transport_leg_alpha. It can be assembled only once? The predicate transport_leg_assembled is true after assembling; effect includes not transport_leg_available. There's no action to disassemble it. So once assembled, it stays assembled. So we can assemble the leg once and reuse for both loading operations. However we need to ensure that loading_container_leg_linked is set correctly for each container. The loading_container_leg_linked predicate links a specific loading container to the transport leg. If we load container_alpha onto leg, we get loading_container_leg_linked loading_container_alpha transport_leg_alpha. If we later load container_beta onto leg, we would need loading_container_leg_linked loading_container_beta transport_leg_alpha. However the predicate loading_container_leg_linked is functional? Not defined as functional, but likely each container can be linked to at most one leg; but a leg could have multiple containers? Not sure. The effect of loading_container_onto_leg adds loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg. It does not remove any previous links. So we could have both containers linked to same leg. That's okay.)
(Thus we can assemble leg once, then load container_alpha onto leg (for sa), verify loading, establish clearance, release compliance. Then load container_beta onto leg (for sb), verify loading, stage candidate (no need for clearance). However note that verify_loading_profile_nominal requires not destination_leg_loaded. We haven't loaded destination leg (no action sets destination_leg_loaded). So fine.)
(Thus we can assemble leg once, then use for both loading operations.)
(Now we need to ensure transport_leg_loading_authorized is true before each loading. The authorize action requires origin_availability_locked and candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile. We have origin_availability_alpha locked (for sb) and also we will have origin_availability_alpha locked for sa? Actually we need origin_availability_locked for the authorize action. The authorize action uses origin_availability (the first argument). It does not require destination_availability? Actually its parameters: ?transport_leg - transport_leg ?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile. Precondition: transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg, origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, not transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_leg. So we need origin_availability_locked (which we have after locking oa). We also need candidate_task_profile_linked for that origin_availability. We'll have attached task profile to oa.)
(Thus we can authorize loading leg using oa as origin_availability. That's fine.)
(Now after we load container_alpha onto leg, we need to verify loading profile for sa. The verify_loading_profile_nominal requires candidate_prepared ?candidate, candidate_skill_certificate_linked ?candidate ?skill_certificate, candidate_operator_linked ?candidate ?operator_resource, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, not destination_leg_loaded ?transport_leg, not candidate_loading_verified ?candidate.)
(Thus we need candidate_skill_certificate_linked for sa? The verify action requires a skill certificate linked to the candidate. So we need to assign skill certificate to sa as well for verification. However goal does not require skill certificate for sa; we can assign and then maybe release after verification? There's release_skill_certificate action. So we could assign skill certificate to sa, verify loading, then release skill certificate (making it available again) for sb later. However goal requires skill_certificate_alpha linked to sb (candidate_skill_certificate_linked shift_candidate_beta skill_certificate_alpha). So we need skill certificate linked to sb at end. We could assign to sa, verify, release, then assign to sb. That works.)
(Alternatively we could use verify_loading_profile_destination_flag which does not require skill certificate? Actually both verify actions require candidate_skill_certificate_linked ?candidate ?skill_certificate (they both have that precondition). Let's check: verify_loading_profile_nominal precondition includes (candidate_skill_certificate_linked ?candidate ?skill_certificate). Yes both have that. So we need skill certificate linked to the candidate for verification.)
(Thus we need skill certificate for sa during verification, then we can release it and assign to sb.)
(Thus we need to manage skill certificate: assign to sa, verify loading, release skill certificate, assign to sb (goal). Also we might need skill certificate for sb's verification? Actually sb does not need verification; we only stage sb (no verification needed). So we can assign skill certificate to sb after releasing from sa.)
(Now we also need compliance certificate for sa's clearance establishment. We'll assign compliance certificate to sa, establish clearance_nominal, then release compliance certificate (making it available). Goal requires compliance_certificate_available at end, so we release after clearance.)
(Now we need to ensure we don't accidentally use compliance certificate for sb (we won't).)
(Now we need to ensure we have loading containers available for each loading action. Initially both loading_containers are available. After loading container_alpha onto leg, it becomes not available. After loading container_beta onto leg, it becomes not available. That's fine.)
(Now we need to ensure we have transport leg assembled before loading. We'll assemble transport leg once after locking oa and da.)
(Now we need to ensure origin_node_ready and destination_node_ready before locking. We'll activate nodes after preparing oa and da.)
(Thus overall plan steps:)
(1. create_candidate origin_availability_alpha)
(2. allocate_vehicle_unit origin_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_alpha (choose any))
(3. attach_task_profile origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(4. confirm_candidate_preparedness origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(5. activate_origin_node origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(6. assign_operator_resource origin_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha)
(7. lock_origin_availability origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha driver_operator_alpha)
(8. release_operator_resource origin_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha (optional, to free operator))
(9. create_candidate destination_availability_alpha)
(10. allocate_vehicle_unit destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta (or reuse after release))
(11. attach_task_profile destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(12. confirm_candidate_preparedness destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(13. activate_destination_node destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(14. assign_operator_resource destination_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha)
(15. lock_destination_availability destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha driver_operator_alpha)
(16. release_operator_resource destination_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha)
(17. create_candidate shift_candidate_alpha)
(18. allocate_vehicle_unit shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma (or reuse after previous releases))
(19. attach_task_profile shift_candidate_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(20. confirm_candidate_preparedness shift_candidate_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(21. assign_compliance_certificate shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha)
(22. assign_skill_certificate shift_candidate_alpha skill_certificate_alpha)
(23. authorize_transport_leg_loading transport_leg_alpha origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(24. load_container_onto_leg shift_candidate_alpha loading_container_alpha transport_leg_alpha)
(25. verify_loading_profile_nominal shift_candidate_alpha skill_certificate_alpha driver_operator_alpha loading_container_alpha transport_leg_alpha)
(26. establish_clearance_nominal shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha loading_container_alpha transport_leg_alpha)
(27. release_compliance_certificate shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha)
(28. release_skill_certificate shift_candidate_alpha skill_certificate_alpha)
(29. finalize_candidate_direct shift_candidate_alpha)
(30. allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(31. execute_schedule_dispatch shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha (or whichever vehicle we allocated))
(32. // Now origin_availability_alpha dispatch)
(33. allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate origin_availability_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(34. execute_origin_dispatch origin_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta dispatch_slot_alpha (or whichever vehicle))
(35. // Destination availability dispatch)
(36. allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate destination_availability_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(37. execute_destination_dispatch destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma dispatch_slot_alpha)
(38. // Now prepare shift_candidate_beta for staging)
(39. create_candidate shift_candidate_beta)
(40. allocate_vehicle_unit shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_alpha (reuse after previous dispatches))
(41. attach_task_profile shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha)
(42. confirm_candidate_preparedness shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha)
(43. assign_operator_resource shift_candidate_beta driver_operator_alpha (goal requires link, we will not release))
(44. assign_skill_certificate shift_candidate_beta skill_certificate_alpha (goal requires link))
(45. // Ensure transport leg is already assembled and loading authorized from earlier steps (still true))
(46. // Load container_beta onto leg)
(47. load_container_onto_leg shift_candidate_beta loading_container_beta transport_leg_alpha)
(48. // Verify loading profile for sb? Not needed for staging, but we might need to verify? Actually stage_schedule_candidate does not require verification. So we can skip verification.)
(49. stage_schedule_candidate shift_candidate_beta loading_container_beta transport_leg_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(50. // Goal achieved.)
(We need to check each action's preconditions are satisfied at the point.)
(Let's go through systematically.)
(We'll need to track state.)
(Initial state:)
(- vehicle_available va, vb, vg)
(- route_task_profile_available rtp)
(- operator_available op)
(- cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha (not used))
(- origin_availability_node_linked oa on)
(- destination_availability_node_linked da dn)
(- transport_leg_available tl)
(- loading_container_available lc_alpha, lc_beta)
(- equipment_available er_alpha, er_beta)
(- service_window_available sw_alpha, sw_beta)
(- dispatch_slot_available ds)
(- skill_certificate_available skill)
(- operational_constraint_available oc_alpha, oc_beta)
(- candidate_operational_constraint_linked sa oc_alpha)
(- candidate_operational_constraint_linked sb oc_beta)
(- candidate_origin_availability_linked sa oa)
(- candidate_origin_availability_linked sb oa)
(- candidate_destination_availability_linked sa da)
(- candidate_destination_availability_linked sb da)
(- candidate_transport_leg_linked sa tl)
(- candidate_transport_leg_linked sb tl)
(- candidate_loading_container_linked sa lc_alpha)
(- candidate_loading_container_linked sb lc_beta)
(- compliance_certificate_available comp)
(All other predicates false.)
(Now step by step.)
(Step1: create_candidate oa)
(Precondition: not candidate_created oa, not dispatched oa. Both false. Effect: candidate_created oa.)
(Step2: allocate_vehicle_unit oa va)
(Precondition: candidate_created oa, not vehicle_allocated oa, vehicle_available va. All true. Effect: vehicle_allocated oa, candidate_vehicle_linked oa va, not vehicle_available va.)
(Step3: attach_task_profile oa rtp)
(Precondition: candidate_created oa, vehicle_allocated oa, route_task_profile_available rtp. All true. Effect: candidate_task_profile_linked oa rtp, not route_task_profile_available rtp.)
(Step4: confirm_candidate_preparedness oa rtp)
(Precondition: candidate_created oa, vehicle_allocated oa, candidate_task_profile_linked oa rtp, not candidate_prepared oa. All true. Effect: candidate_prepared oa.)
(Step5: activate_origin_node oa on rtp)
(Precondition: candidate_prepared oa, candidate_task_profile_linked oa rtp, origin_availability_node_linked oa on, not origin_node_ready on, not origin_node_occupied on. We have origin_availability_node_linked oa on true from init. origin_node_ready? initially false. origin_node_occupied? false. So ok. Effect: origin_node_ready on.)
(Step6: assign_operator_resource oa op)
(Precondition: candidate_prepared oa, operator_available op. operator_available? Initially true. Effect: candidate_operator_linked oa op, not operator_available op.)
(Step7: lock_origin_availability oa on op)
(Precondition: candidate_prepared oa, candidate_operator_linked oa op, origin_availability_node_linked oa on, origin_node_ready on, not origin_availability_locked oa. All true. Effect: origin_availability_locked oa, origin_availability_confirmed oa.)
(Step8: release_operator_resource oa op)
(Precondition: candidate_operator_linked oa op. Effect: operator_available op, not candidate_operator_linked oa op.)
(Now after step8, operator is available again.)
(Step9: create_candidate da)
(Precondition: not candidate_created da, not dispatched da. True. Effect: candidate_created da.)
(Step10: allocate_vehicle_unit da vb)
(Precondition: candidate_created da, not vehicle_allocated da, vehicle_available vb. vb is still available (we haven't used it). Effect: vehicle_allocated da, candidate_vehicle_linked da vb, not vehicle_available vb.)
(Step11: attach_task_profile da rtp)
(Precondition: candidate_created da, vehicle_allocated da, route_task_profile_available rtp? Wait we used rtp earlier for oa and it became not available after attach_task_profile. So route_task_profile_available is now false. We need a route_task_profile for da as well. But we only have one route_task_profile_alpha object. It can be linked to multiple candidates? The predicate route_task_profile_available indicates availability; after linking, it becomes not available. However we might be able to link same route_task_profile to multiple candidates? The attach_task_profile action's effect includes not route_task_profile_available ?route_task_profile. It does not require that the route_task_profile be unlinked from other candidates. So linking to multiple candidates would make it not available each time, but after first link it's already not available; second link's precondition requires route_task_profile_available, which would be false. So we cannot attach the same route_task_profile to multiple candidates unless we have multiple copies. We only have one route_task_profile_alpha. So we need to reuse it? Actually we might not need to attach task profile to da for lock actions? Let's check lock_destination_availability precondition: candidate_prepared ?destination_availability, candidate_operator_linked ?destination_availability ?operator_resource, destination_availability_node_linked ?destination_availability ?destination_node, destination_node_ready ?destination_node, not destination_availability_locked ?destination_availability. It does not require candidate_task_profile_linked. So we don't need to attach task profile to da for lock. However we need candidate_prepared da, which requires candidate_task_profile_linked da rtp (as per confirm_candidate_preparedness). So we need to attach task profile to da to become prepared. But we cannot attach because rtp is not available after we attached to oa.)
(Thus we need another route_task_profile? Not provided. However we could maybe not need to confirm candidate_preparedness for da if we don't need it for lock? Wait lock_destination_availability requires candidate_prepared ?destination_availability. So we need candidate_prepared. That requires candidate_task_profile_linked. So we need to attach a task profile to da. But we only have one rtp. However maybe we can use the same rtp for multiple candidates if we detach it after use? There's detach_task_profile action that removes the link and makes route_task_profile_available again. So we could attach rtp to oa, then later detach it from oa (making it available) then attach to da. But we need oa to retain its task profile link for other purposes (like authorize_transport_leg_loading requires candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile). That uses origin_availability (oa). So we need oa to keep its task profile link. However we could detach after we have done authorize and loading? Actually authorize_transport_leg_loading uses origin_availability (oa) and requires candidate_task_profile_linked oa rtp. So we need that link to persist at least until we authorize loading. After that, we might not need it further. So we could detach after authorize.)
(Thus we can attach rtp to oa, then later detach it after we have done authorize_transport_leg_loading (or after we have completed all steps needing oa's task profile). Then we can attach rtp to da.)
(Similarly we need rtp for sa and sb for various steps (prepare, confirm preparedness, maybe for authorization? Actually authorize uses origin_availability only, not the schedule candidate. So sa and sb do not need task profile linked for authorization. However confirm_candidate_preparedness for sa and sb requires candidate_task_profile_linked. So we need rtp linked to sa and sb as well. So we need rtp for four candidates: oa, da, sa, sb. But we can detach and reattach as needed, as long as we have it available when needed.)
(Thus we need to manage rtp availability.)
(We have only one rtp object. We'll need to attach/detach as needed.)
(We also need to assign operator to oa and da for lock steps, and to sb for goal.)
(We need to assign skill certificate to sa for verification, then release, then assign to sb.)
(We need to assign compliance certificate to sa for clearance, then release.)
(We need to load container_alpha onto leg for sa's verification and clearance, then load container_beta onto leg for sb's staging.)
(We need to assemble transport leg once (after locking oa and da). The assemble_transport_leg action requires origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_availability_node_linked, destination_availability_node_linked, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available.)
