(Now we have sa ready for dispatch: we need to finalize candidate (make dispatch_ready). We used finalize_candidate_direct after clearance. That action requires candidate_clearance_established sa, not route_sequence_context_set sa, not candidate_finalized sa. Wait finalize_candidate_direct precondition includes NOT route_sequence_context_set ?candidate. But after establish_clearance_nominal we set route_sequence_context_set sa (effect includes route_sequence_context_set ?candidate). So we cannot use finalize_candidate_direct after establishing clearance_nominal because route_sequence_context_set becomes true, violating the not condition. Indeed finalize_candidate_direct requires NOT route_sequence_context_set. So we need to use finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation instead, which requires route_sequence_validated ?candidate. Or finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation requires compliance_validation_complete ?candidate. We haven't done compliance validation. Or we could avoid establishing clearance_nominal and instead use establish_clearance_origin_loaded or destination_loaded or full_load, which also set route_sequence_context_set. All clearance actions set route_sequence_context_set (look at their effects). So after any clearance action, route_sequence_context_set becomes true. Then we cannot use finalize_candidate_direct (which requires not route_sequence_context_set). So we need to use finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation or finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation.)
(Let's examine those:)
(- finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation: precondition candidate_clearance_established ?candidate, route_sequence_validated ?candidate, not candidate_finalized ?candidate. Effect: candidate_finalized ?candidate, dispatch_ready ?candidate.)
(- finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation: precondition compliance_validation_complete ?candidate, not candidate_finalized ?candidate. Effect: candidate_finalized ?candidate, dispatch_ready ?candidate.)
