(- finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation sa (requires compliance_validation_complete sa, not candidate_finalized sa). Effect: candidate_finalized sa, dispatch_ready sa.)
(- allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate sa ds rtp (requires dispatch_ready sa, candidate_task_profile_linked sa rtp, dispatch_slot_available ds, not dispatch_allocated sa))
(- execute_schedule_dispatch sa va ds (or whichever vehicle we allocated))
(- release_compliance_certificate sa comp (to make it available))
(- release_skill_certificate sa skill (if we assigned skill certificate earlier for verification? Actually we might not need skill certificate for sa if we go via compliance validation path; we don't need skill certificate for sa at all. The verify_compliance_certificate does not require skill certificate. So we can avoid using skill certificate for sa altogether, leaving it free for sb. Good! That simplifies.)
